# Model Tier Routing — Porteos Intelligence

## Installed local models (M2 Max, 32GB — free, no API cost)

| Model | Size | Speed | Best for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `qwen2.5-coder:7b` | 4.7 GB | ~60 tok/s | Tier 1 fast edits |
| `phi4-mini:latest` | 2.5 GB | ~80 tok/s | Tier 1 trivial tasks |
| `qwen2.5-coder:14b` | 9.0 GB | ~40 tok/s | Tier 2 feature work |
| `deepseek-r1:14b` | 9.0 GB | ~30 tok/s | Tier 2 reasoning/planning |
| `gemma4:12b` | 7.6 GB | ~35 tok/s | Tier 2 general alternative |

## Paid models (Cursor subscription — use sparingly)

| Model | When |
|---|---|
| `Sonnet 4.6` | Tier 3 only — high-risk files, schema, security, concurrency |

---

## Tier decision + model prompt

At the START of every response involving code changes, state the tier and prompt the user to switch:

```
// TIER 1 → switch to: qwen2.5-coder:7b or phi4-mini
// TIER 2 → switch to: qwen2.5-coder:14b
// TIER 2 REASONING → switch to: deepseek-r1:14b
// TIER 3 → stay on Sonnet 4.6
```

---

## Tier 1 — qwen2.5-coder:7b or phi4-mini (free, ~60–80 tok/s)

Single file, data/config/copy only:
- `MarketBenchmarks.swift` — adding cities, adjusting rates
- `MarketFeedRegistry.swift` — adding feeds, aliases
- `DealPropertyTypes.swift` — adding property types
- `DealTemplates.swift` — adding/editing templates
- `PorteosGlossary.swift` — glossary entries
- `LLMAnalysisService.swift` — prompt text edits only (not routing logic)
- `UnitSystemService.swift` — adding currency/country mappings
- `PorteosScoreCalculator.swift` — weight/threshold adjustments only
- `BrowserExtension/**` — JavaScript scraper updates
- `DealExporter.swift` — column reordering, format strings
- `BetaGuide.md` or any `.md` file — documentation
- Any single-view label, color token, or copy change

## Tier 2 — qwen2.5-coder:14b (free, ~40 tok/s)

2–5 files, logic changes, clear scope:
- Dashboard views (`RealEstateDashboardView`, `HospitalityDashboardView`, etc.)
- `NewsAggregatorService.swift` + `MarketFeedRegistry.swift` together
- `SensitivityAnalysisBlock.swift` — calculation changes
- `PreloadReviewSheet.swift`, `BatchTriageView.swift`
- `PDFReportGenerator.swift` — layout changes
- `MarketTrendGrid.swift` — metric changes
- `GeocodingService.swift` — query or fallback logic
- `NavigationPane.swift` — UI additions
- `SettingsView.swift` — new settings sections
- `CompactDealInspector.swift`, `DealMediaGalleryView.swift`
- `GeoPortfolioMapView.swift`, `GeoAssetContextCard.swift`
- `GlobalIntelligenceInspectorViews.swift`
- Bug fixes in files under 600 lines with clear scope
- Browser extension: adding a new portal scraper

## Tier 2 Reasoning — deepseek-r1:14b (free, ~30 tok/s)

Use when you need to THINK before coding:
- Diagnosing a non-obvious bug
- Planning a multi-file feature before implementation
- Architecture decisions
- Interpreting TestFlight feedback / crash logs

## Tier 3 — Sonnet 4.6 (paid, ~$3–5/session — use sparingly)

ONLY for these high-risk files or categories:

**Never touch with Tier 1/2:**
- `FullDealEditSheet.swift` (1,274 lines)
- `AIVibePanel.swift` (1,149 lines)
- `AIAnalysisService.swift` (989 lines)
- `AppShell.swift` — core layout / window management
- `PropertyDeal.swift` — SwiftData schema (data loss risk)
- `DealHistoryManager.swift` — snapshot/undo system
- `EmailMonitorService.swift` — IMAP + async + Keychain
- `DealIngestionServer.swift` — HTTP server protocol changes

**High-risk categories (always Tier 3):**
- SwiftData `@Relationship` or `@Model` changes
- Security: Keychain, API key handling, network auth
- Concurrency: `async`/`await`, `@MainActor`, actor isolation
- Multi-window: `WindowManager`, `ProfileWindowView`, `WindowGroup`
- Onboarding flow
- Swift 6 concurrency compliance
- Anything cascading across 5+ files

---

## Quick decision

```
Single file, data/config/copy?         → TIER 1 (qwen2.5-coder:7b)
Need to reason through a problem?      → TIER 2 REASONING (deepseek-r1:14b)
2–5 files, logic changes, clear scope? → TIER 2 (qwen2.5-coder:14b)
High-risk file OR schema/security?     → TIER 3 (Sonnet 4.6)
```

## Estimated monthly cost at this split

- 60% Tier 1 · 30% Tier 2 · 10% Tier 3 = **$3–10/month**
- Local models: $0 (electricity only)
